{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>She is more righteous.</b> Than I — by her words." "<b>From me.</b> She is pregnant. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, drashed that a bat kol went out and said: 'From Me and from him the matter came forth' — for she was modest in the house of her father-in-law; I decreed that kings should come forth from her, and from the tribe of Yehudah I decreed to establish kings in Israel." "<b>Because therefore I did not give her.</b> For she did justly, in that I did not give her to Shelah my son." "<b>And he did not again.</b> Some say: he did not add. And some say: he did not cease. And its fellow is by Eldad and Medad: וְלֹא יָסָפוּ — and the Targum renders it: וְלָא פְּסָקוּ."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:40.791386033Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}